<title>UK: Grand Met's Burger King to buy UK beef.</title>
<headline>Grand Met's Burger King to buy UK beef.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamburger chain Burger King, owned by Grand Metropolitan Plc, said on Tuesday it would resume purchases of British beef that it halted last year following a scare over mad cow disease.</p>
<p>Market leader McDonald's made a similar move on June 26.</p>
<p>Burger King said consumer confidence in British beef had recovered to the point at which it was able to start using it again in its fast food restaurants.</p>
<p>&quot;Seventy-three percent of our customers now support a move back to British beef which has the added reassurance of the farm-approved scheme and traceability,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
</text>
